# React Frontend Patterns

## Component Structure

### Functional Components
- Always use functional components with hooks
- Use `export default` for page components
- Use named exports for reusable components

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD
function PlayerCard({ player }) {
  return <div>{player.name}</div>;
}

export default PlayerCard;
```

### File Organization
- **Pages**: `frontend/src/pages/` - Route-level components
- **Components**: `frontend/src/components/` - Reusable UI components
- **Services**: `frontend/src/services/` - API calls and utilities

## API Integration

### Using the API Service
- Always use functions from `services/api.js` for API calls
- Never make direct `fetch` or `axios` calls in components
- Handle loading and error states

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { getLeague } from '../services/api';

function LeagueDashboard() {
  const [league, setLeague] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    getLeague(id)
      .then(setLeague)
      .catch(setError)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, [id]);
}
```

### Error Handling
- Always catch API errors and display user-friendly messages
- Show loading states during API calls
- Handle empty states gracefully

## React Router

- Use `react-router-dom` for routing
- Routes defined in `App.jsx`
- Use `useParams()` to get route parameters
- Use `useNavigate()` for programmatic navigation

## State Management

- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useEffect` for side effects (API calls, subscriptions)
- Pass data down via props, lift state up when needed
- No global state management library (keep it simple)

## Styling

- Use inline styles for simple styling: `style={{ margin: '20px' }}`
- Use className for CSS classes when needed
- Keep styles close to components

## Best Practices

- Keep components small and focused
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks if needed
- Use descriptive prop names
- Handle edge cases (empty arrays, null values, etc.)
